  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Spit. Two-player simultaneous shedding; play face-up stock cards onto either centre spit pile when next in sequence up or down; turn stock cards face up or move to empty space; when blocked both spit again; first to empty all stock wins the round then slap for pile choice; first to get rid of all cards wins the game.',
    Player: "Spit (or 'Slam') is a fast-paced two-player shedding card game related to Speed. Unlike Speed, each player maintains five small 'stock piles' in front of them (similar to Solitaire layout) and races to empty these piles onto two central discard stacks. Play is simultaneous and chaotic. The winner of a round gets to choose the smaller pile for the next round, aiming to start with fewer cards.",
    objective: 'Get rid of all your cards. Or have fewer cards at the end.',
    gameplay: "Both players shout 'spit' and flip their top spit card to start two centre spit piles. Play is simultaneous with no turns. Each player may: play a face-up stock card onto either spit pile if it is next in sequence up or down (suit and colour do not matter; ace may play on 2 or king); turn the top card of a stock pile face up; or move a face-up stock card into an empty stock space. When neither can play, both shout 'spit' again and each turns their next spit card onto their pile. When one player empties all stock piles or play is blocked with no spit cards left, players slap to choose a pile; each takes their chosen pile, adds remaining cards, shuffles, and deals a new layout. First to get rid of all cards wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Play onto a spit pile only if your card is next in sequence up or down; suit and colour do not matter; ace connects to 2 and king.',
      'Only one card may be moved at a time.',
      "When neither can play, both shout 'spit' and each turns the next spit card onto their pile.",
      'First to empty all stock piles wins the round; then players slap to choose which centre pile to take for the next deal.',
      'If a player has fewer than 15 cards they cannot deal a full layout and there is only one spit pile; first to empty stock takes nothing, the other takes the centre.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two players only. Play is simultaneous with no turns; physical speed and alertness are required to play faster than the opponent.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Shuffle well and divide the pack equally so each player receives 26 cards; no jokers.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck only.',
      dealing: 'Shuffle and divide the deck equally (26 cards each). Each player deals five stock piles in a row: first pile 1 card, second 2, third 3, fourth 4, fifth 5. Deal face down then turn the top card of each pile face up. The remaining 11 cards per player stay face down as the spit cards.',
    },
    turnFlow: "Both players shout 'spit' and flip their top spit card to start two centre spit piles. Play is simultaneous with no turns. Each player may: play a face-up stock card onto either spit pile if it is next in sequence up or down (suit and colour do not matter; ace may play on 2 or king); turn the top card of a stock pile face up; or move a face-up stock card into an empty stock space. When neither can play, both shout 'spit' again and each turns their next spit card onto their pile. When one player empties all stock piles or play is blocked with no spit cards left, players slap to choose a pile; each takes their chosen pile, adds remaining cards, shuffles, and deals a new layout. First to get rid of all cards wins.",
